    "body": "@pseudo-su I have a somewhat strange question for you. What happens if you set `CLOUDSDK_ACTIVE_CONFIGE_NAME` to null/empty string? Does `gloud` CLI fallback to reading active config from `active_config` file or what?\r\n\r\nThe reason I'm asking you that is we could solve this by saying if `CLOUDSDK_ACTIVE_CONFIG_NAME` is set to null ie. (active config) name length is zero don't display gcloud module. If `CLOUDSDK_ACTIVE_CONFIG_NAME` is not present at all use the `active_config` file. Otherwise, use its value. How does that sound? Totally or just slightly crazy? :smile: ",
